# interplay_limits_ranges_depth3: Guest RAM in 16 ranges: the first, and 15 of 8 pages each with a range-sized hole after each, listed to the device in reverse order (the memory map sorts them). Three tasks of 32 GiB (0x800000000, the in-process maximum) share one depth-3 page table (the deepest) whose tables, task roots and data pages are dealt out over the 15 ranges in turn: the first eight VA pages (object list, records, command buffers) in the first range, and 16 two-page buffers at VA pages 0x8000 k + 0xfff, each across two leaf tables and so across two ranges. Each task runs one exec of 16 fills over all 16 buffers: task 1 across each buffer's page boundary, task 2 at its start, task 3 at its end. Every page of every buffer lands in its own range, in every setup (no run of pages crosses a range, so the blocks setup maps each as it is).
